Subject: [PATCH 4/4] OW-09: Nota Ambil Aksesori lists the whole note history
 (D17-16)

The screen sends history_status, history_order, history_offset and
history_limit with its search; the stage's accessory reader applies them to
every matching note before the page is cut. The status select and the order
start again at the first page; "Nota sebelumnya/berikutnya" move through the
server pages; the count line shows the server's count of the whole filtered
history; the tool text says "Filter dan urutan berlaku untuk seluruh hasil".
No client-side filtering or ordering is left.

parseAccessoryWorkspace takes the requested page and refuses, closed, a
history_page that is missing, extra, for another offset/limit/list, with a
row of another status, or whose next page disagrees with the count; and a
history_page the request did not ask for.

The three page-only oracles move to D17-16 keeping their intent: a reorder
keeps unsent quantities and the selected note (now one server read with the
editor context), the wording names its real scope, and Browse resets every
list key while keeping the form. New tests cover paging, status/search
starting at page 1, and the refusals.

